  "description": "Description of the Proposal \nThe proposal involves the removal of a metal external fire escape staircase located at the east elevation of the building serving flat 32 connecting it to the roof. The staircase is no longer required as part of the current fire safety and evacuation strategy for the building. Its removal will not compromise fire escape provision within the building and will enhance both safety and the appearance of the east elevation.\n\nFollowing the removal of the fire escape, the affected section of tiling will be reinstated with tiles to match the existing. The parapet in this area will also be extended and rebuilt to align with the height and detailing of the surrounding parapet.\n\nFire Safety Statement \nThis application relates to the removal of a redundant external fire escape staircase at Esmond Court. A review of the building's fire strategy has confirmed that the staircase is no longer required as part of the approved means of escape. Internal escape routes fully comply with current fire safety regulations and provide adequate protection and egress for residents in the event of an emergency.\n\nThe external staircase is currently in a state of disrepair and presents a potential hazard. Its removal will eliminate the associated structural and safety risks without impacting the building’s fire safety integrity.\n\nThe proposal does not involve any changes to internal layouts or fire compartmentation, and there will be no reduction in the level of fire protection afforded to occupants. All works will be carried out in accordance with the Regulatory Reform (Fire Safety) Order 2005 and in consultation with the building’s responsible person or fire risk assessor, where applicable.",
